body: "At `b919f35bc280f0ef29fce05b1b4a865887f29244`, the [scheduled Node 26/Bun job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/45012114155/job/137176480632) waited unassigned for 9h 29m 41s. Once assigned, checkout, install and strict health passed, but the full release gate reported `the c8 coverage run exceeded its 3600000 ms deadline`. The interrupted test receipt showed 825 passed, 39 cancelled and zero assertion failures; partial coverage is not a pass. The [previous push at the same commit](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/44927333228) had three deadline failures and one successful Node 26/Bun leg on a different runner. This evidence does not establish OOM or any particular host or resource bottleneck.\n\nThe [quick/deep design](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/79) retains comprehensive tests and full four-dimension coverage in each deep leg. The [job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b919f35bc280f0ef29fce05b1b4a865887f29244/.github/workflows/ci-deep.yml#L15-L29) has 120 minutes, but [c8](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b919f35bc280f0ef29fce05b1b4a865887f29244/scripts/coverage-gate.ts#L250-L280) separately has 60 minutes and two test workers. Reuse [the native CI coverage item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b919f35bc280f0ef29fce05b1b4a865887f29244/.agents/pm/issues/pm-swarm-9bks.toon), whose older reporter heap incident is distinct from the evidence here.\n\nAcceptance: measure queue wait separately from execution, and use stage timings, peak memory and actual termination reasons from comparable runs before adding more CI load. Demonstrate complete deep gate receipts with time headroom for eligible runners, or document routing the heavy gate to a runner class that can finish it. Preserve existing required checks, coverage scope and thresholds, install acceptance and strict health. An incomplete run must not become a success.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (3)\n\n> **@coderabbitai[bot]** (2026-11-22T21:35:22Z)\n>\n> <!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n> \n> <!-- This is an auto-generated issue plan by CodeRabbit -->\n> <details>\n> <summary>🔗 Related PRs</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> unbraind/pm-swarm#65 - Recover close after ownership transfer and interrupted native lifecycle [merged]\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary>📝 Issue Planner</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> <sub>Check the box below or use the `@coderabbitai plan` command to generate an implementation plan and prompts that you can use with your favorite coding assistant.</sub>\n> \n> - [ ] <!-- {\"checkboxId\":\"8d4f2b9c-3e1a-4f7c-a9b2-d5e8f1c4a7b9\"} --> Create Plan\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> \n> ---\n> <details>\n> <summary> 🧪 Issue enrichment is currently in open beta.</summary>\n> <dl>\n> <dd>\n> <br>\n> \n> \n> You can configure auto-planning by selecting labels in the issue_enrichment configuration.\n> \n> To disable automatic issue enrichment, add the following to your `.coderabbit.yaml`:\n> ```yaml\n> issue_enrichment:\n>   auto_enrich:\n>     enabled: false\n> ```\n> </dd>\n> </dl>\n> </details>\n> \n> 💬 Have feedback or questions? Drop into our [discord](https://discord.gg/coderabbit)!\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-22T23:21:47Z)\n>\n> A second Node 26 leg on the same Pi 4B reproduced not just the deadline but the same test frontier: [npm](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/45012114155/job/137176480863) and [Bun](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/45012114155/job/137176480632) both reached 825 passing tests, 39 cancellations and no assertion failures before the 60-minute watchdog. The Node 22/npm leg also reported the c8 deadline.\n> \n> The most useful first profile is [the close-crash matrix](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/blob/b919f35bc280f0ef29fce05b1b4a865887f29244/test/close-crash-matrix.test.ts#L6): the 1-, 2- and 3-dependent cases passed in about 8, 12 and 16 minutes in each Node 26 leg. Those three cases accounted for roughly 36 minutes of reported case time, while the two-worker run still had the privacy-admission and punctuation suites active when the timeout interrupted it. These are case durations, not an additive profile across concurrent files. This narrows the next comparison to test/subprocess cost and fixture reuse before blaming coverage reporting or raising the cap; no OOM or product runtime regression established.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-22T23:35:22Z)\n>\n> Triaged 2026-11-22: queued as agent round `pm-swarm-97-1123`. It reproduces the issue first, then builds the acceptance criteria with revert-proven tests."
